<article class="env-lemma" id="08AQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08AQ">Lemma <span data-tag="08AQ">69.20.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Consider a commutative diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ X \ar[r]_ i \ar[rd]_ f &  \mathbf{P}^ n_ Y \ar[d] \\  &  Y }  \]
</div>
  <p> of algebraic spaces over $S$. Assume $i$ is a closed immersion and $Y$ Noetherian. Set $\mathcal{L} = i^*\mathcal{O}_{\mathbf{P}^ n_ Y}(1)$. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a coherent module on $X$. Then there exists an integer $d_0$ such that for all $d \geq d_0$ we have $R^ pf_*(\mathcal{F} \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ X} \mathcal{L}^{\otimes d}) = 0$ for all $p > 0$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Checking whether $R^ pf_*(\mathcal{F} \otimes \mathcal{L}^{\otimes d})$ is zero can be done étale locally on $Y$, see Equation (<a href="/tag/071Z" data-tag="071Z">69.3.0.1</a>). Hence we may assume $Y$ is the spectrum of a Noetherian ring. In this case $X$ is a scheme and the result follows from Cohomology of Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/02O1" data-tag="02O1">30.16.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>